From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 21:23:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00349/11171] [outer-loop] P1 v2 INCONCLUSIVE (guard caught
 starved positive control); root cause diagnosed; conductor resumed.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

P1 v2 ran clean (5150s, no crash) but ar_best=0.000 again — every method (ar/argmin/
descent/beam) floored at 0. The ar_best<0.3 guard correctly returned INCONCLUSIVE rather
than falsely claiming FUNDAMENTAL off a failed positive control (the v1 trap, now prevented
by design). Root cause: this harness hardcoded n_train=min(20000,...) while the scaled
harness that achieved AR=0.84 uses min(40000,...). 20k examples starve the from-scratch AR
on 3-digit MSD-first addition. Fixed to 40000; stale 20k checkpoint removed so a future v3
retrains correctly. Corrigendum stamped on the artifact.

This is the 3rd long P1 run (v1 small-model degenerate, v2 eval crash, v2-rerun n_train bug).
Conductor was paused ~4h for P1 — past the "don't leave it paused indefinitely" line — so
resumed it (PID 182505) and deferred the corrected v3 (one-line fix, ~100min) to an operator
decision. Energy-as-generator remains BOUNDED from part-b regardless; P1 only sharpens the
artifact-vs-fundamental mechanism, it does not change the strategic conclusion.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
